## 9. Images

Use `DrawImage` to place PNG or JPEG images.

```csharp
page.DrawImage("assets/logo.png", x: 100, y: 500);
page.DrawImage("assets/photo.jpg", x: 260, y: 500, width: 180, height: 120);

var fit = page.DrawImageFit("assets/hero.png", x: 100, y: 320, maxWidth: 240, maxHeight: 140);
var centered = page.DrawImageFitCenter("assets/icon.png", x: 360, y: 320, maxWidth: 120, maxHeight: 120);
page.DrawImageScaledToWidth("assets/banner.png", x: 360, y: 320, width: 180);
```

Behavior:
- If `width`/`height` are omitted, intrinsic pixel dimensions are used as PDF points.
- Aspect helpers preserve ratio:
  - `DrawImageScaledToWidth(...)`
  - `DrawImageScaledToHeight(...)`
  - `DrawImageFit(...)`
  - `DrawImageFitCenter(...)` (fit + centered in bounding box)
- Supported formats:
  - JPEG (`DCTDecode`)
  - PNG, non-interlaced, 8-bit grayscale/RGB, with optional alpha (`FlateDecode` + PNG predictor)
- PNG alpha is mapped to PDF soft mask (`/SMask`).
- Unsupported PNG variants (palette/interlaced) throw `NotSupportedException`.

