## 15. Links

Add a clickable web link area to a page:

```csharp
page.DrawText("Open .NET docs", x: 100, y: 700, fontSize: 14);
page.AddWebLink(x: 100, y: 696, width: 140, height: 18, url: "https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/");

// Internal page navigation (1-based page index)
page.AddPageLink(x: 260, y: 696, width: 110, height: 18, targetPageNumber: 2);
```

Notes:
- Link rectangle uses PDF coordinates (bottom-left origin).
- Web links are exported as `/Subtype /Link` annotations with `/URI` actions.
- Page links are exported as `/Subtype /Link` annotations with `/Dest` page targets.

---

## 16. Bookmarks

Add entries to the PDF navigation pane:

```csharp
document.AddBookmark("Page 1 - Shapes", 1);
document.AddBookmark("Page 2 - Details", 2);
```

Notes:
- Page numbers are 1-based.
- Bookmarks are exported as PDF outline items (`/Outlines`).

---

## 17. Table of Contents

Generate table-of-contents pages from existing bookmarks:

```csharp
document.AddBookmark("Page 1 - Shapes", 1);
document.AddBookmark("Page 2 - Details", 2);

document.AddTableOfContents(new PdfTableOfContentsOptions
{
    Title = "Contents",
    FontFamily = PdfFontFamily.Helvetica,
    EntryFontSize = 11
});
```

Notes:
- TOC entries are clickable and use internal page links.
- Long bookmark lists automatically continue onto additional TOC pages.

---

## 18. Save Options

Enable content stream compression:

```csharp
document.Save("output.pdf", new PdfSaveOptions
{
    CompressContentStreams = true
});
```

Notes:
- Compression uses `/Filter /FlateDecode` on page content streams.
- Images keep their own format-specific filters.

Export variants:

```csharp
// File
document.Save("output.pdf", new PdfSaveOptions { CompressContentStreams = true });

// Stream
using var stream = File.Create("output-stream.pdf");
document.Save(stream, new PdfSaveOptions { CompressContentStreams = true });

// Bytes
var bytes = document.ToBytes(new PdfSaveOptions { CompressContentStreams = true });
File.WriteAllBytes("output-bytes.pdf", bytes);
```

